      },
      "message": "fix(project): a loaded stock keeps its geometry revision\n\nset_facets bumps an entity's geometry revision on every landing. The\nproject loader pinned it back to the file's value for models but not for\nstocks, so a stock set twice saved \"rev\": 2, loaded as rev 1, and the\nre-save differed from the file it was opened from. The Stock arm now pins\nrev after set_facets, unconditionally like the Model arm (an absent key\npins 0, matching older files). Staleness never reads rev; this removes\nfile-byte churn on open-and-save.\n\nPinned by project_roundtrip::stock_set_twice_keeps_its_rev_across_save_load_save.\n\nFixes #340\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
